 3. 🌐 World reconsiders America 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Axios Visuals

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 America is shedding its status as the default choice for foreign governments to park money, buy weapons and send students.

 Why it matters: Even modest shifts away from the U.S. could chip away at advantages that have helped sustain American economic and geopolitical power for decades, Axios' Neal Rothschild writes. European countries are looking for ways to wean off the U.S.:

 Weapons: Europe is seeking to source more equipment locally to reduce its dependence on American firepower, Reuters reports. Tech: The EU this summer set out plans to reduce its reliance on American companies, drafting cloud rules that would restrict Amazon, Google and Microsoft from competing for sensitive contracts, Reuters also reported . 🎓 Zoom out: International applications to U.S. colleges dropped 10% in the most recent admissions cycle. Travel to America fell 5.5% in 2025, including 25% drops in visitors from both Canada and Germany.

