 4. 📚 Library hotspots 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Institute of Museum and Library Services Public Libraries Survey . Map: Sami Sparber/Axios Americans checked out an average of 6.5 books, e-books and other materials from public libraries in 2024, Axios' Sami Sparber writes from federal data. 

 Ohioans, Utahns and Washingtonians are the biggest library fans. They lead the nation with 11+ checkouts per person. U.S. library circulation is rebounding from its pandemic-era drop , largely thanks to a boom in digital borrowing . Share this map . 

 
 
